  "video_notes": [
    "Scene time t maps to video time start_s + t. Clips before a fade/zoom-in are recorded past duration_s by the next transition duration; xfade offset = next start_s, so each scene starts on its start_s.",
    "SC-01 opens with a 0.5 s fade from black; the video ends with a 0.5 s fade to black (96.0-96.5 s).",
    "SC-01 eases its camera back to 1.0x over its last 0.9 s so the same-screen fade into SC-02 does not double-expose two framings.",
    "SC-05 re-ticks 3 and 4 Oct (at_s 0.0/0.2) behind the settle marker, so the first frame already shows both days ticked (no unticked flash at the cut).",
    "SC-08 opens already at its 1.6x camera framing; the zoom-in transition is a camera push in SC-07 tail footage plus a 0.4 s cross-fade (ffmpeg xfade zoomin washed out to near-white). After Continue to payroll navigates, the camera eases back to 1.0x over 0.6 s.",
    "Cursor position carries over from the end of each scene into the next."
  ]
